            <ArticleTitle>Primary lymph node gastrinoma: a rare cause of abdominal pain in childhood.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/MPH.0b013e318298de7e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastrinoma is a hormone-secreting tumor associated with the Zollinger-Ellison syndrome. It is quite rare among children. The discovery of gastrinomas in unusual locations such as lymph nodes, bones, ovaries, and the liver poses a diagnostic dilemma as to whether the tumor is primary or metastatic. Here, we present a case of a primary gastrinoma within a lymph node.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
